      "body": "The structure of Western religion is a Simplex structure of the Heaven–Earth–Human triad. Of the Ten Commandments, the 1st–4th concern Heaven, the 5th–7th Earth, and the 8th–10th mainly speak of Human. The 「Lord's Prayer」 likewise: 'Hallowed be thy name (Heaven),' 'Give us this day our daily bread (Earth),' 'Forgive us our sins as we have forgiven those who have sinned against us (Human).' Even in the temptation by Satan unfolded over 40 days in the wilderness, Jesus refused the miracle of turning stones into bread and thus conformed to the order of Heaven (Heaven), rejected the temptation of being given all the kingdoms of the world (Earth), and refused the test of throwing himself down from the temple (Human) (한태동, 『사유의 흐름』, 2003, pp.50-54). In that Jesus readily expressed the source of the Heaven–Earth–Human triad with the word 'Father,' he also accords with Confucianism."
